      "value": "@{680f1496b78da8b5132f3f14|full_name} Since you asked what I expect — ideally, I’d like the brightness to be at least closer to ToonLit, because the current Toon Standard is simply too bright. In fact, even ToonLit tends to blow out highlights easily, so it would be best if the shader could avoid overexposure more effectively.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
    {
      "__v": 0,
      "_id": "682169b5158d828d2c46f852",
      "aiGenerated": false,
      "author": {
        "_id": "60ffe11e9425ef064dcd9ef5",
        "alias": "International orange Locust",
        "aliasID": "65c2e908ed6eefce4c4202ec",
        "anonymized": false,
        "avatarURL": "https://canny-assets.io/images/4825832d41a79010ebfd5eed5fa82b00.png",
        "created": "2021-07-27T10:34:06.233Z",
        "name": "lilxyzw",
        "serviceAccount": false,
        "urlName": "lilxyzw"
      },
      "authorID": null,
      "boardID": "5b0746088fa72313783e3269",
      "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
      "created": "2025-05-12T03:23:33.620Z",
      "deleted": false,
      "deletedAt": null,
      "fileURLs": [],
      "files": [],
      "imageURLs": [],
      "integrationSourceType": null,
      "internal": false,
      "itemSourceType": null,
      "mentionedUserIDs": null,
      "mentionedUsers": [],
      "mergeID": null,
      "parentID": null,
      "pinned": false,
      "postDeleted": false,
      "postID": "681ec123b2bce50666550b08",
      "private": false,
      "reactions": {
        "like": 2
      },
      "restoredAt": null,
      "sourceFeatureExtractionItemID": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "This issue can be divided into two problems.\n\nThe first is that there is a difference in Light Probe brightness between the two shaders. Toon Lit calculates the average (which is actually slightly different), while Toon Standard calculates the brightest point, so there is a difference in brightness. I think this is as specified, but I think it would be appropriate for the two shaders to have the same brightness to increase the sense of immersion.\n\nThe second is that the brightness of Toon Standard exceeds 1.0. This shader adds a clamped directional light and a light probe. However, the result of adding the two is not clamped, so the brightness will exceed 1.0 and spoil the appearance of the texture. I think this user wants the result of adding the directional light and the light probe together to be clamped.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
