          "avatarURL": "https://canny-assets.io/images/4825832d41a79010ebfd5eed5fa82b00.png",
          "created": "2021-07-27T10:34:06.233Z",
          "name": "lilxyzw",
          "serviceAccount": false,
          "urlName": "lilxyzw"
        }
      ],
      "mergeID": null,
      "parentID": "682169b5158d828d2c46f852",
      "pinned": false,
      "postDeleted": false,
      "postID": "681ec123b2bce50666550b08",
      "private": false,
      "reactions": {
        "like": 5
      },
      "restoredAt": null,
      "sourceFeatureExtractionItemID": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{60ffe11e9425ef064dcd9ef5|full_name}: That does make sense, thanks for the investigation!\n\nThe brightest-point sampling is indeed intentional, as it tends to give a more toon-style shading in our experience with worlds. I don't expect that part to change.\n\nClamping the final result instead of the intermediary light calculations might make sense though, and probably solve this issue for most cases. I will look into that!",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
